## Structs

### struct `Config`

```rust
#[must_use]
pub struct Config<T = ()> {
    pub extra: T,
    pub mode: Mode,
    // some fields omitted
}
```

[source](https://github.com/example/repo/blob/0123abc/src/lib.rs#L90-L96)

Runtime configuration.

Built with [`Config::new`](latest-basic#fn-confignew). See the [`Mode`](latest-basic#enum-mode) enum, [the util module](latest-basic-util), and
[a reference-style link](latest-basic-util#fn-helper).

#### Errors

Never fails.

**Fields**

- `pub extra: T`

  User supplied extra data.
- `pub mode: Mode`

  How to run.

#### fn `Config::new`

```rust
impl<T: Default> Config<T> {
    pub fn new(name: &str) -> Self;
}
```

[source](https://github.com/example/repo/blob/0123abc/src/lib.rs#L104-L106)

Creates a config with the given name.

```rust
let c = basic::Config::<()>::new("x");
```

#### fn `Config::name`

```rust
impl<T> Config<T> {
